        <!-- Hero -->
        <section class="how-hero">
            <div class="how-hero-text">
                <span class="eyebrow">Swiss Trails Algorithm</span>
                <h1>What is it?</h1>
                <p>
The application allows you to find a near optimal path through popular swiss trail heads, minimizing the total distance between them. This is a traveling salesman combinatorial problem, where we treat trail heads as nodes and the path between them as edges in a graph problem.  We have implemented the Ant Colony Optimization problem, which is especially good at solving the traveling salesman problem, and created visualizations to allow you to visualize the artificial ants creating their potential solution paths (in blue), highlighting the best path found so far (orange). 
                </p>

                <a class="how-button" href="/">Try the route finder</a>
            </div>

            <figure class="how-photo hero-photo">
                <img src="/assets/allTrailsCropped.png" alt="Swiss trail map n=359">
                <figcaption>ACO on all 359 trailheads after 100 iterations</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </section>


        <!-- Overview Cards -->
        <section class="how-section">
            <div class="section-heading">
                <span class="eyebrow">Process</span>
                <p>
                    Each ant creates a possible route. Over time, better routes become more likely
                    because they receive more pheromone.
                </p>
            </div>

