            <div class="code-grid">
                <article class="code-card">
                    <h3>1. Distance between two trail points</h3>
                    <p>
                        The Haversine formula calculates the distance between two latitude and longitude points.
                    </p>

                <pre><code>function haversine(p1, p2) {
                    const R = 6371;

                    const phi1 = p1.latitude * Math.PI / 180;
                    const phi2 = p2.latitude * Math.PI / 180;

                    const dphi = (p2.latitude - p1.latitude) * Math.PI / 180;
                    const dlambda = (p2.longitude - p1.longitude) * Math.PI / 180;

                    const a = Math.sin(dphi / 2) ** 2 +
                            Math.cos(phi1) * Math.cos(phi2) *
                            Math.sin(dlambda / 2) ** 2;

                    const c = 2 * Math.atan2(Math.sqrt(a), Math.sqrt(1 - a));

                    return R * c;
                }</code></pre>
                </article>

                <article class="code-card">
                    <h3>2. Choosing the next trail point</h3>
                    <p>
                        Ants prefer nearby points and paths with stronger pheromone.
                    </p>

<pre><code>const tau = pheromone[current][j] ** alpha;
const eta = (1 / distanceMatrix[current][j]) ** beta;
const score = tau * eta;</code></pre>
                </article>

                <article class="code-card">
                    <h3>3. Building all ant routes together</h3>
                    <p>
                        Promise.all lets all ants visually build their routes at the same time.
                    </p>

<pre><code>const antSolutions = await Promise.all(
    Array.from({ length: m }, (_, a) =>
        buildAntRoutes(
            a,
            iter,
            nodes,
            pheromone,
            distanceMatrix,
            alpha,
            beta,
            seed
        )
    )
);</code></pre>
                </article>
            </div>
